 variety of conditions, including those related to malnutrition, highlighting their broad application in the healthcare payment framework.\",2\r\n3301,CLASIFICACIÓN INTERNACIONAL DE ENFERMEDADES,\"The Clasificación Internacional de Enfermedades (CIE), known in English as the International Classification of Diseases (ICD), is an international instrument developed by the World Health Organization (WHO) to identify health trends and statistics worldwide. This system is utilized for coding and classifying diseases and health conditions, providing a standardized framework for health data collection and analysis across different countries and healthcare systems.\",1\r\n3310,GERIATRIC PATIENTS,Geriatric patients are older adults who may be at risk of malnutrition and are the focus of various studies and nutritional strategies.,1\r\n3302,GUERRA RS,A researcher involved in studies related to malnutrition and its impact on health outcomes.,1\r\n8026,BAKER,\"Baker is a prominent researcher known for significant contributions to the field of nutrition. He co-authored a study focused on sucrose digestion in patients, enhancing the understanding of carbohydrate metabolism. Additionally, Baker played a key role in the development of the Global Subjective Assessment method, which is utilized for nutritional evaluation, providing a comprehensive approach to assessing an individual's nutritional status. Furthermore, he is recognized for developing the classic VGS method in the 1980s, which has been instrumental in evaluating nutritional status. Through these contributions, Baker has made a lasting impact on nutritional research and assessment methodologies.\",2\r\n8025,VGS-GP,\"The VGS-GP is a variation of the original VGS method, designed for use in oncology patients to assess nutritional status with patient involvement.\",1\r\n12629,NATIONAL ALLIANCE FOR INFUSION THERAPY,The National Alliance for Infusion Therapy is an organization that addresses issues related to infusion therapy 